{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 9, 19]], "date-time": "2025-09-19T07:11:28Z", "timestamp": 1758265888650}, "reference-count": 59, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "5", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2016, 8, 17]], "date-time": "2016-08-17T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1471392000000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/termsAndConditions#vor"}], "funder": [{"DOI": "10.13039/501100002347", "name": "Bundesministerium f\u00fcr Bildung und Forschung", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["0315414"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["0315414"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100002347", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["Plant Breeding"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2016, 10]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title><jats:p>Grain yield and its component trait thousand kernel weight are important traits in triticale breeding programmes. Here, we used a large mapping population of 647 doubled haploid lines derived from four families to dissect the genetic architecture underlying grain yield and thousand kernel weight by multiple\u2010line cross <jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">QTL</jats:styled-content> mapping. We identified 3 <jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">QTL</jats:styled-content> for grain yield and 13 for thousand kernel weight which cross\u2010validated explained 5.2% and 48.2% of the genotypic variance, respectively. Both traits showed a positive phenotypic correlation, and we found two <jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">QTL</jats:styled-content> overlapping between them. Full two\u2010dimensional epistasis scans revealed epistatic <jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">QTL</jats:styled-content> for both traits, suggesting that epistatic interactions contribute to their genetic architecture. Based on <jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">QTL</jats:styled-content> identified in our results, we conclude that the potential for marker\u2010assisted selection is limited for grain yield but more promising for thousand kernel weight.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1111/pbr.12400", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2016, 8, 17]], "date-time": "2016-08-17T08:08:42Z", "timestamp": 1471421322000}, "page": "567-573", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 17, "title": ["Multiple\u2010line cross <scp>QTL</scp> mapping for grain yield and thousand kernel weight in triticale"], "prefix": "10.1111", "volume": "135", "author": [{"given": "Wenxin", "family": "Liu", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Crop Genetics and Breeding Department China Agricultural University Beijing 100193 China"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Willmar L.", "family": "Leiser", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "State Plant Breeding Institute University of Hohenheim Stuttgart 70599 Germany"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Jochen C.", "family": "Reif", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Leibniz Institute of Plant Genetics and Crop Plant Research (IPK) Gatersleben 06466 Germany"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Matthew R.", "family": "Tucker", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "School of Agriculture, Food and Wine University of Adelaide Waite Campus Urrbrae SA 5064 Australia"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Dominik", "family": "Losert", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "State Plant Breeding Institute University of Hohenheim Stuttgart 70599 Germany"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Sigrid", "family": "Weissmann", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "HegeSaat GmbH &amp; Co.KG Singen\u2010Bohlingen 78224 Germany"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "cros